        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "specifically a NodeJS REST API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 96.661,
          "en": "And in case this doesn't tell you anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.661,
          "end": 99.75,
          "en": "this and the next videos probably isn't for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.75,
          "end": 102.72,
          "en": "But nonetheless, in case this doesn't tell you anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "NodeJS is kind of like a programming language you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "actually it's using JavaScript as a programming language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "But NodeJS is a runtime that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "to run JavaScript outside of the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.99,
          "en": "And in order to build and run a NodeJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.99,
          "end": 124.92,
          "en": "you therefore must install NodeJS on your system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "It is available for all operating systems and platforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "and if you visit NodeJS.org,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "you can download the LTS or this very latest version there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 137.16,
          "en": "Of course, the versions might differ",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.16,
          "end": 138.87,
          "en": "at the point of time you are watching this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "but simply download your LTS version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 144.81,
          "en": "So whatever is displayed for you here and you are fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.81,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "It should automatically pick your Operating System.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 150.42000000000002,
          "en": "If it doesn't, you can click on other downloads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.42000000000002,
          "end": 153.57,
          "en": "and manually pick the installer for your version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.57,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "for your Operating System.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 158.34,
          "en": "And then you simply go through that installer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "which you can download here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "and this will install NodeJS on your system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "So that's NodeJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 168.51,
          "en": "A REST API in the end is a website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "without any visible pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 174.57,
          "en": "Instead, it's just about providing some URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.57,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "to which users or applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "can send requests to exchange data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 183.42,
          "en": "REST APIs are often used behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.42,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "by mobile apps, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 189.63,
          "en": "where the mobile app provides the visual user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.63,
          "end": 192.63,
          "en": "and behind the scenes talks to such a REST API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 194.7,
          "en": "to exchange data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "Now we're going to build a meetups REST API here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 199.59,
          "en": "in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.59,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "And this meetups REST API which we are going to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "will be relatively simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 209.057,
          "en": "but nonetheless contains some crucial features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.057,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "which you will very likely encounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 214.56,
          "en": "in any REST API you might be building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.56,
          "end": 217.05,
          "en": "Now this REST API we are about to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 219.36,
          "en": "or which I want you to build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.36,
          "end": 222.75,
          "en": "should have four main endpoints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 226.77,
          "en": "It should have a post slash meetups endpoint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.77,
          "end": 231.77,
          "en": "so a slash meetups URL endpoint that accepts POST requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 235.005,
          "en": "which would be used to create a new meetup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.005,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "so which accepts incoming user data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.2,
          "en": "to then create and store a new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.2,
          "end": 244.16,
          "en": "And POST requests are simply one kind of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.16,
          "end": 248.673,
          "en": "officially supported HTTP request types, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "In addition to this post slash meetups route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 256.59,
          "en": "the API also should support a GET slash meetups route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 260.91,
          "en": "which would be used to fetch those stored meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 262.59,
          "en": "And we also wanna have a PATCH",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 266.25,
          "en": "and DELETE slash meetups slash ID route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.25,
          "end": 269.25,
          "en": "which updates an existing meetup by ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.25,
          "end": 272.37,
          "en": "or deletes an existing meetup by ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.37,
          "end": 276.21,
          "en": "And if the ID here will actually be a dynamic segment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.21,
          "end": 279.3,
          "en": "since different meetups will have different IDs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 279.3,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "and they should be targetable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "by including their IDs in the URLs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "so in this slash meetups slash ID path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 291.87,
          "en": "Again, if this doesn't tell you anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.87,
          "end": 294.84000000000003,
          "en": "it might still be interesting to watch these videos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.84000000000003,
          "end": 298.47,
          "en": "but you should definitely gain this basic programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 300.09,
          "en": "and web development knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.09,
          "end": 303.06,
          "en": "before trying this task on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.06,
          "end": 307.02,
          "en": "So these are the endpoints this REST API should have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.02,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "and every meetup that's going to get created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 312.42,
          "en": "in that post route or that's going to be fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 314.7,
          "en": "as part of the whole list of meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 317.31,
          "en": "in the GET route, should have a title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.31,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "a summary, an address, and an ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 323.79,
          "en": "So these data points should make up a meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.79,
          "end": 326.19,
          "en": "And title, summary and address are simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 326.19,
          "end": 327.886,
          "en": "short pieces of text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.886,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "The ID could be a number or a text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.81,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "that's totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 335.07,
          "en": "All that meetup data should then be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 335.07,
          "end": 338.58,
          "en": "in a meetups.json file inside of the project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 338.58,
          "end": 341.01,
          "en": "In reality, you might be using a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 341.01,
          "end": 345.3,
          "en": "but to keep this demo simple and make it not too complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 345.3,
          "end": 348.57,
          "en": "we'll just use a meetups.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.57,
          "end": 352.05,
          "en": "And all the incoming data that's about to be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 352.05,
          "end": 355.11,
          "en": "should be validated before being stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 355.11,
          "end": 357.33,
          "en": "So you should for example, have some logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 357.33,
          "end": 359.88,
          "en": "that makes sure that the title and the summary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.88,
          "end": 362.31,
          "en": "and the address are not empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 364.68,
          "en": "so that there is some text in these fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 364.68,
          "end": 367.47,
          "en": "that the user did submit some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.47,
          "end": 370.98,
          "en": "In addition, JSON should be used as a data format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 370.98,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "not just for storing these meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 375.48,
          "en": "in this meetups.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 375.48,
          "end": 378.72,
          "en": "but also for sending them back in a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 378.72,
          "end": 380.85,
          "en": "to these incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 380.85,
          "end": 382.47,
          "en": "And that's the basic definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 382.47,
          "end": 384.69,
          "en": "for this example of REST API here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 384.69,
          "end": 387.96,
          "en": "That is the kind of REST API we will build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 387.96,
          "end": 390.27,
          "en": "over the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 390.27,
          "end": 393.03,
          "en": "Now, just as before, with the example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 393.03,
          "end": 395.716,
          "en": "for people without programming experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 395.716,
          "end": 398.73,
          "en": "I then also got some enhancements for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 398.73,
          "end": 402.54,
          "en": "For example, once you finished that basic REST API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 402.54,
          "end": 405.24,
          "en": "you should add authentication to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 405.24,
          "end": 409.44,
          "en": "so that you have two additional routes slash signup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 409.44,
          "end": 413.90999999999997,
          "en": "and slash login, which both accept POST requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 413.90999999999997,
          "end": 417.42,
          "en": "which are used to create users and log users in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 417.42,
          "end": 419.31,
          "en": "And users should simply be defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 419.31,
          "end": 423.03,
          "en": "as a combination of an email and a password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 423.03,
          "end": 425.85,
          "en": "The authentication should be JWT-based,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 425.85,
          "end": 430.05,
          "en": "so JSON Web Token based, and once the authentication routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 430.05,
          "end": 433.02,
          "en": "have been added, you should then also add logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 433.02,
          "end": 436.59,
          "en": "to protect all other routes except for GET meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 436.59,
          "end": 438.84,
          "en": "so that only authenticated requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 438.84,
          "end": 442.02,
          "en": "so requests sent by users who did log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 442.02,
          "end": 444.75,
          "en": "are allowed to those other routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 444.75,
          "end": 447.57,
          "en": "So to the POST, PATCH and DELETE routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 447.57,
          "end": 449.852,
          "en": "these three routes should be protected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 449.852,
          "end": 452.31,
          "en": "once you added authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 452.31,
          "end": 454.92,
          "en": "And again, if this all doesn't tell you anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 454.92,
          "end": 457.05,
          "en": "because you got no programming experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 457.05,
          "end": 460.32,
          "en": "or maybe simply no web development experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 460.32,
          "end": 462.87,
          "en": "simply feel free to just watch the videos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 462.87,
          "end": 467.4,
          "en": "to see how such an application could be built with ChatGPT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 467.4,
          "end": 469.74,
          "en": "Another enhancement which I have for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 469.74,
          "end": 471.99,
          "en": "is to add error handling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 471.99,
          "end": 476.49,
          "en": "which simply means that in different parts of the REST API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 476.49,
          "end": 479.55,
          "en": "you should make sure that errors are thrown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 479.55,
          "end": 482.767,
          "en": "For example, if user input validation fails",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 482.767,
          "end": 486.21,
          "en": "or if a user tries to access a protected route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 486.21,
          "end": 488.07,
          "en": "without being authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 488.07,
          "end": 491.4,
          "en": "and you should set up a generic error handling middleware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 491.4,
          "end": 493.86,
          "en": "as part of your REST API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 493.86,
          "end": 496.5,
          "en": "So some general error handling function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 496.5,
          "end": 499.2,
          "en": "that is triggered whenever an error is thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 499.2,
          "end": 501.3,
          "en": "anywhere in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 501.3,
          "end": 505.23,
          "en": "And that middleware should then send back error responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 505.23,
          "end": 508.26,
          "en": "with appropriate response status codes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 508.26,
          "end": 512.19,
          "en": "For example, a 401 status code if the problem is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 512.19,
          "end": 515.07,
          "en": "that a user tried to access a protected route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 515.07,
          "end": 516.903,
          "en": "without being authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 518.19,
          "end": 519.72,
          "en": "These are the enhancements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 519.72,
          "end": 523.32,
          "en": "But of course, just as before, definitely first start",
